438
00:55:06.680 --> 00:55:22.620
Nadine Loepfe: As you have seen, and you can create your own copy of that branch, and you can make as many changes as you want. So you can literally think of it like a tree, with different branches. Now, the thing is, as soon as you're happy with these branches, you kind of want to

439
00:55:23.080 --> 00:55:39.200
Nadine Loepfe: want to put it back into the tree. Otherwise, you just go… go off and have your next branches from there. But what we really want to do, of course, is that these changes that you make are coming back to the trunk. So, how you're doing this is, of course, with raising a pull request.

